 (273, 'Let us think and reflect – I (Extract) & II', [
  'I. i. She likes rocks and stones more than lush green plants – an unusual taste. ii. True. iii. A path made of irregular, uneven stones laid in no fixed pattern. iv. A. She has a fascination with unusual items.',
  'II 1. She loves and is proud of it – she thinks the sundial “rather nice”, invites the speaker to see her stones and talks about a flower for a quarter of an hour.',
  'II 2. To show humorously how tiny and delicate the plants are – they are hardly visible among the stones.',
  'II 3. She is proud, enthusiastic, patient and friendly; she loves unusual things and notices small beauties that others miss.',
  'II 4. She is shown as cheerful, hospitable (invites her neighbour), passionate about her garden and calm – she does not get angry when he steps on her flower.',
  'II 5. People value things differently – what is precious to one person (a tiny flower) may look ordinary to another.',
  'II 6. As a garden full of stones with a crazy path, lily pond, rockery and strange sundial; the description creates amusement and curiosity.',
  'II 7. Because the plants are so small that they seem unimportant to him; it shows his careless, slightly mocking attitude at first.',
  'II 8. It reveals that the garden has real, precious plants hidden among the stones and that the speaker had not noticed them – the joke is on him.']),
